{"text": "When Aunt Em came there to live, she was a young, pretty wife. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> But the sun and wind had changed her, too. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> They had taken the sparkle from her eyes and left them a sober gray. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> She was thin and pale now, and she never smiled. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> When Dorothy, who was an orphan, first came to her, the childs laughter startled Aunt Em. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Aunt Em would scream and press her hand on her heart whenever she heard the girls merry voice. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> She still looked at Dorothy and wondered how the girl could find anything to laugh at. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Uncle Henry never laughed, for he worked hard from morning till night. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> He was gray from his long beard to his rough boots, and he rarely spoke. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> It was Toto that made Dorothy laugh and saved her from growing as gray as everything else. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Toto was a little black dog with long, silky hair and small black eyes that twinkled merrily. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Toto played all day long, and Dorothy played with him and loved him dearly.", "alignment": {"characters": ["W", "h", "e", "n", " ", "A", "u", "n", "t", " ", "E", "m", " ", "c", "a", "m", "e", " ", "t", "h", "e", "r", "e", " ", "t", "o", " ", "l", "i", "v", "e", ",", " ", "s", "h", "e", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "a", " ", "y", "o", "u", "n", "g", ",", " ", "p", "r", "e", "t", "t", "y", " ", "w", "i", "f", "e", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "B", "u", "t", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "s", "u", "n", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "w", "i", "n", "d", " ", "h", "a", "d", " ", "c", "h", "a", "n", "g", "e", "d", " ", "h", "e", "r", ",", " ", "t", "o", "o", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "T", "h", "e", "y", " ", "h", "a", "d", 